.TH PSYCHOD 1 "July 2026" "i3psycho 1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
psychod \- companion daemon for i3psycho, the floating-first i3
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B psychod
[\fB\-\-cascade\-step\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-edge\-margin\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-drop\-debounce\fR \fIS\fR]
[\fB\-\-hot\-corners\fR \fISPEC\fR]
[\fB\-\-hot\-corner\-size\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-hot\-corner\-delay\fR \fIS\fR]
[\fB\-\-auto\-hide\-bars\fR \fIEDGES\fR]
[\fB\-\-bar\-class\fR \fIREGEX\fR]
[\fB\-\-bar\-slide\-ms\fR \fIN\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B psychod
implements the macOS-style window behaviors of i3psycho over the i3 IPC
protocol: cascade placement of new windows, exact-workarea snapping,
minimize with geometry restore, an expose grid, MRU window cycling, show
desktop, hot corners, and auto-hiding bars. It is a pure IPC client: if it dies, the window
manager is unaffected. It is normally started from the i3 config:
.PP
.nf
    exec_always --no-startup-id flock -n /tmp/psychod-${DISPLAY#:}.lock psychod
.fi
.PP
Actions are triggered by
.B nop psycho:<action>
keybindings or
.B i3\-msg \-t send_tick psycho:<action>
from scripts. Actions: snap:left|right|max|center|tl|tr|bl|br, min,
restore[:con_id], cycle, expose, showdesktop.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-cascade\-step " " \fIN\fR
Pixel offset between cascaded window spawns (default 30).
.TP
.BR \-\-edge\-margin " " \fIN\fR
Pixels beyond the workarea edge that trigger poll-based drop snapping
(default 25). The patched i3 also snaps natively during drags.
.TP
.BR \-\-drop\-debounce " " \fIS\fR
Seconds a moved window must rest before snapping (default 0.25).
.TP
.BR \-\-hot\-corners " " \fISPEC\fR
Comma-separated corner=action pairs from tl, tr, bl, br (default
"tl=expose,br=showdesktop"), or "none" to disable. Requires xdotool.
.TP
.BR \-\-hot\-corner\-size " " \fIN\fR
Size in px of the square at each corner that arms it (default 8). One
pixel is unhittable in practice; raise this on a HiDPI screen.
.TP
.BR \-\-hot\-corner\-delay " " \fIS\fR
Seconds the pointer must rest in the corner before it fires (default 0.5).
.TP
.BR \-\-auto\-hide\-bars " " \fIEDGES\fR
Edges whose bar hides until the pointer touches that edge: "top",
"bottom", "top,bottom", or "none" (default). The bar must be
override-redirect, else i3 owns its placement and reverts the slide:
polybar
.BR "override-redirect = true" ,
i3bar
.BR "mode hide" .
An override-redirect bar reserves no space, so windows use the whole
output. Requires xdotool.
.TP
.BR \-\-bar\-class " " \fIREGEX\fR
X class regex matching bars to auto-hide (default "polybar|i3bar").
.TP
.BR \-\-bar\-slide\-ms " " \fIN\fR
Slide duration in ms (default 140); 0 snaps with no animation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR i3 (1),
.BR i3\-msg (1)
.PP
Full guide: /usr/share/doc/i3psycho/userguide.txt
.SH AUTHOR
The i3psycho project (https://github.com/ekruges/i3psycho).
